{"game": "warframe", "language": "english", "appid": 230410, "month": "2019-04", "window": 1, "start_date": 1554076800, "end_date": 1554681599, "month_true_total": 983, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-14 18:58:45 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "50022019", "author": {"steamid": "76561198268232003", "personaname": "Zhanna", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/JustShrimp/", "num_games_owned": 236, "num_reviews": 172, "playtime_forever": 61042, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 53, "playtime_at_review": 44994, "last_played": 1789200149, "avatar": "69cd3d107516397316a2d8f642b574a58849cd63"}, "language": "english", "review": "okay.  after a few billion hours of warframe i have many things to say.\n\nfirst off. warframe is a game with alot of lore, so it will be a headache to attempt to talk about all of it, but some of the lore kinda ♥♥♥♥ over the other parts of lore, rabbit holes and paradox's all over the place, i wish the devs would try and fix those but clearly its alittle more complicated then i would have originally have thought of. \n\nsecond. when starting out the game you are just kinda thrown into the world not really explained what you need to do. as most people don't follow along and lets be real. most won't bother to read, so i would like if there was a way to explain to starters a better way to start and where to go.\n\nthird. the actual support team is insanely fast and kind. i had my account stole and sold on some random site. giving some information and purchases was all i needed to get my account back rather fast. \n\nthere is many things to love and hate about the game. i can recommend it, but i highly would like if you do start playing this game, please for the love of god just understand you gotta make it to mars for the real game to begin", "timestamp_created": 1554681193, "timestamp_updated": 1756193519, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score"